            <ArticleTitle>Atherosclerotic aneurysm of the left main coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1062-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A large calcified atherosclerotic aneurysm of the left main coronary artery was successfully treated by aortocoronary saphenous vein bypass grafting. This is the second such reported case. The implications of this clinical entity are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
